        "reason": "The source identity 'Arabia Petraea' refers to the Roman province created by Trajan in AD 106, while Galatians 1:17 and 4:25 only say 'Arabia' during Paul's earlier first-century context. Those Greek tokens correctly belong to broader place:Arabia. They cannot prove a reference to a Roman province which did not yet exist. Retain the historic geographic identity as post-biblical context.",
